---
import { studies } from "../../../data/studies";
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";
---

<StudyLayout>
	{studies.map((study) => (
		<article>
			<p>
				{study.phase} · {study.status}
			</p>
			<h2>
				<a href={`/lab/studies/${study.slug}`}>{study.title} →</a>
			</h2>
			<p>{study.question}</p>
		</article>
	))}
	<p>
		Studies have four parts: design problem → exploration → readiness →
		integration plan. Readiness assesses feasibility; integration documents how
		and why to implement the conclusion. Study-quality evaluation is separate.
		Status records exploratory → accepted → integrated into shared
		implementation. Acceptance does not imply implementation. Closed studies
		retain their evidence; consult their closure record for the final outcome.
	</p>
</StudyLayout>
<style>
article {
	border: var(--flight-border);
	padding: var(--spacing-lg);
	margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
	background: var(--color-void-light);
}
</style>
